            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Rosa mandonii is a species of flowering plant in the family Rosaceae, native to Madeira. Some authorities consider it to be indistinguishable from Rosa canina, the dog rose. It is most often found in the laurisilva, but can also occur in other types of woodland and in thickets."
